+# Research
+
+## Request path and current behavior
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/category/CategoryApi.java` maps `DELETE /api/v1/private/category/{id}` to `CategoryFacade.deleteCategory(Long, MerchantStore)`.
+- `CategoryFacadeImpl.deleteCategory(Long, MerchantStore)` currently calls a private `getOne` method that invokes the generic `categoryService.getById(categoryId)` (a JPA `getOne` reference) without checking the merchant store. A missing ID can therefore fail while resolving a proxy instead of becoming the API's normal `ResourceNotFoundException`/404.
+- `CategoryFacadeImpl.getById` uses a language-specific category lookup for `GET /api/v1/category/{id}` and throws `ResourceNotFoundException` when it returns null. Product listing by category and category-product variants also resolve the category and are expected to return no results/404 after deletion.
+
+## Deletion cause
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/category/CategoryServiceImpl.java` builds the deleted category's descendant set from its lineage, finds products in those category IDs, and then:
+  - removes categories only when a product has more than one category;
+  - deletes the product when it has one category, or when the remaining-category check is based on the stale `product` object;
+  - deletes only the root category explicitly, relying on `Category.categories`'s `CascadeType.REMOVE` for children.
+- This directly explains products, inventory, prices, cart references, and order references disappearing. `ProductServiceImpl.delete` removes product associations and then cascades product-related data, so it is the wrong operation for category deletion.
+- The correct ownership direction is `Product.categories` in `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/catalog/product/Product.java`: a lazy `@ManyToMany` through `PRODUCT_CATEGORY`. Products must remain managed and have only the deleted category IDs removed from this set.
+- `Category` in `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/catalog/category/Category.java` models children with `@OneToMany(mappedBy="parent", cascade=CascadeType.REMOVE)`. Descendant categories and their descriptions should be removed, while product rows must not be removed.
+
+## Other affected behavior
+
+- `CategoryRepository.findByLineage` is used to discover descendants and category product listings. Once the category and descendants are deleted, those queries naturally stop returning them; product-category join rows must also be removed so product detail responses no longer expose deleted categories.
+- Cart and order models reference product/order-product data, not category membership. Keeping the `Product` entity and updating only its category set preserves stock, price, carts, and order history.
+- `ProductServiceImpl.getProducts(List<Long>)` delegates to `ProductRepositoryImpl.getProductsListByCategories`, which currently uses fetch joins for product data. It is used by the faulty delete flow and is sufficient for normal products, but deletion should never call `ProductService.delete`.
+- Existing tests include `sm-core/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/catalog/CategoryTest.java` and category API integration coverage in `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/category/CategoryManagementAPIIntegrationTest.java`; neither currently asserts product preservation, descendant detachment, or missing-category DELETE behavior. Hidden/request-level tests are likely to exercise those cases.
+
+## Intended change
+
+1. Resolve the category by merchant-scoped ID and raise `ResourceNotFoundException` when absent.
+2. Collect the root and all descendants, remove those category objects from every affected product, and persist the products.
+3. Delete descendant categories and then the root, without deleting any product.
+4. Verify with focused tests/build commands and, if possible, add regression coverage for product preservation and 404 behavior.
